<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month t-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month t-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 9.606 percent on Monday from 9.921 percent at the previous auction on March 17.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 879.875 million pounds, replace bills worth 860.550 million maturing on Tuesday . The treasury had asked for 800 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Oct 7, 1997 (Sept 16, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.606 percent (9.921)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 879.875 million (878.175 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,820.275 million (1,676.650 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.000-9.641 percent (9.501-9.999)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.000-10.050 percent (9.701-10.101)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 54 (55)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 197 (177)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
